'' ON ERROR GOTO, in the shape fbc emits. See the source.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -exx --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/onerror.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' THE HANDLER IS A BLOCK ADDRESS, and blockaddress names the function it is in --
'' a block address means nothing outside the function that owns the block.
'' EXPECT-OUT: call ptr @"fb_ErrorSetHandler"(ptr blockaddress(@"RISKY"
'' ...and the check's result is TESTED and JUMPED THROUGH, not discarded.
'' EXPECT-OUT: indirectbr ptr
'' EVERY REACHABLE BLOCK IS LISTED: LLVM verifies that set, and an omitted destination
'' is a module it refuses -- an empty list would let the optimiser drop the handler.
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare ptr @"fb_ErrorSetHandler"
